        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://copperharbor.org/activities-recreation/historic-locations/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Fort Wilkins Historic State Park sits just east of downtown; it was built in 1844 to defend the copper port from Ojibwe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copper_Harbor%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic Copper Harbor Lighthouse, one of Lake Superior’s oldest, was decommissioned in 1933 and now serves as a museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copper_Harbor%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Isle Royale Queen IV ferry operates from Copper Harbor each summer, a legacy of the former Isle Royale Ferry Service.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copper_Harbor%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
